   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "UNET + text encoder: Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3 (or any repack \u2014 int8 convrot builds work too). Pair the Ref2VA PDD file with a ref2va UNET, FL2VA with fl2va.\n\nPDD Acc file goes in models/pdd_acc/ \u2014 either the original alibaba-pai/MiniMax-H3-Acc-LoRAs release or the pre-converted ComfyUI copy (aptech0081/MiniMax-H3-Acc-LoRAs-ComfyUI). Both load.\n\nOptional: wire reference images into ref_image_0... for identity-locked r2v."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    390,
    700
   ],
   "size": [
    430,
    330
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 5,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "TWO-PHASE WARMUP (split sigma):\nPhase 1 = BASE-model guider (no PDD, no distill LoRAs) runs the warmup steps sigma 1.0 \u2192 handoff for composition/identity. Phase 2 = the PDD guider finishes from the handoff on the trained tail (0.8 \u2192 2 PDD evals; pick a higher handoff_sigma for more PDD evals \u2014 see its tooltip).\n\nThe Warmup Scheduler's sigmas are split by SplitSigmas at its phase2_start_step output; pass 1's OUTPUT latent (not denoised_output) chains into pass 2 with DisableNoise \u2014 no re-noising between passes.\n\nThe PDD Apply node's own sigmas output is UNUSED here (that is the single-phase recipe). Its enabled/bypass_sigmas inputs are a full-bypass toggle, unrelated to this split. Keep the Apply node at nfe 8 so the tail stays on the block-4 grid.\n\neuler both passes, CFG 1.0, SigmaShift 12/3."
   ],
   "title": "Two-phase recipe"
  },
